WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.155
- He won the Mr. Universe
contest when he was 20,

00:00:03.155 --> 00:00:06.250
and the Mr. Olympia contest seven times.

00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:09.452
He is worth hundreds
of millions of dollars.

00:00:09.452 --> 00:00:12.393
He's been an athlete, actor, entrepreneur,

00:00:12.393 --> 00:00:15.419
director, model, and politician.

00:00:15.419 --> 00:00:17.163
He's Arnold Schwarzenegger and here

00:00:17.163 --> 00:00:19.197
are his ten rules for success.

00:00:19.197 --> 00:00:21.280
(swoosh)

00:00:22.747 --> 00:00:26.628
- Here's the goal, and whatever it takes

00:00:26.628 --> 00:00:28.711
to get there, I would do.

00:00:32.868 --> 00:00:34.603
So, I was doing my daily work,

00:00:34.603 --> 00:00:37.221
cleaning the guns, going
to the shooting range,

00:00:37.221 --> 00:00:40.056
marching 20 miles a day and falling around

00:00:40.056 --> 00:00:43.575
up hills with weapons,
running at five in the morning

00:00:43.575 --> 00:00:45.393
with heavy combat boots
and all this stuff,

00:00:45.393 --> 00:00:47.714
and then everyone just almost drops dead

00:00:47.714 --> 00:00:49.622
at night, is totally exhausted.

00:00:49.622 --> 00:00:52.592
I worked out three hours and got up early

00:00:52.592 --> 00:00:54.175
in the morning again to do my sit-ups,

00:00:54.175 --> 00:00:57.475
and the push-ups, and my chin-ups.

00:00:57.475 --> 00:01:00.086
There was a clear conflict, a dilemma.

00:01:00.086 --> 00:01:02.281
Because the lifting was not a traditional

00:01:02.281 --> 00:01:05.206
sport for them, they didn't like the idea.

00:01:05.206 --> 00:01:06.961
They didn't even have the equipment.

00:01:06.961 --> 00:01:08.977
I had to go and figure
out every way possible

00:01:08.977 --> 00:01:11.386
to do dips with chairs, or put a bar

00:01:11.386 --> 00:01:15.136
across two chairs, and
do upside down rowing.

00:01:17.771 --> 00:01:19.430
Everyone would say this
is the wrong direction

00:01:19.430 --> 00:01:21.418
that I'm going, or I'm in a dream world,

00:01:21.418 --> 00:01:25.207
I'm useless, whatever it
was, I'm going to break

00:01:25.207 --> 00:01:28.097
through that, no matter what it takes.

00:01:28.097 --> 00:01:30.902
I needed to reach that goal.

00:01:30.902 --> 00:01:32.657
That vision that I had,

00:01:32.657 --> 00:01:34.824
of being a world champion.

00:01:36.741 --> 00:01:37.993
Think big.

00:01:37.993 --> 00:01:40.118
Because then you're going to get big.

00:01:40.118 --> 00:01:42.146
Then you're going to go
and achieve big things.

00:01:42.146 --> 00:01:43.751
That is the most important thing.

00:01:43.751 --> 00:01:46.175
We don't achieve big things by accident.

00:01:46.175 --> 00:01:49.802
So, shoot for the top, shoot for the sky.

00:01:49.802 --> 00:01:51.469
Shoot for the stars.

00:01:53.144 --> 00:01:55.436
All of those liabilities
that they talked about

00:01:55.436 --> 00:01:57.332
that are turning into assets.

00:01:57.332 --> 00:01:58.934
When I did Conan the Barbarian

00:01:58.934 --> 00:02:00.562
the director came to me and he said,

00:02:00.562 --> 00:02:02.470
If we wouldn't have you, we would

00:02:02.470 --> 00:02:04.303
have had to build one.

00:02:05.642 --> 00:02:07.657
And on Terminator, the director said,

00:02:07.657 --> 00:02:10.332
I couldn't imagine to have anyone play

00:02:10.332 --> 00:02:12.319
Terminator that wouldn't have an accent

00:02:12.319 --> 00:02:15.243
and that wouldn't have your body.

00:02:15.243 --> 00:02:17.383
I cannot imagine the line "I'll be back."

00:02:17.383 --> 00:02:19.795
with a normal American accent.

00:02:19.795 --> 00:02:22.657
It worked so perfectly that
you have this German accent.

00:02:22.657 --> 00:02:23.998
So all of those things that

00:02:23.998 --> 00:02:27.802
they say are liabilities, became an asset.

00:02:27.802 --> 00:02:30.728
As moment went on, I grew and grew

00:02:30.728 --> 00:02:33.113
and went from one movie to the next,

00:02:33.113 --> 00:02:34.913
started making more and more money

00:02:34.913 --> 00:02:38.204
and then I ended up being
the highest paid actor

00:02:38.204 --> 00:02:42.132
with 30 million dollars in Terminator 3.

00:02:42.132 --> 00:02:44.965
(German dialogue)

00:03:00.395 --> 00:03:02.312
- [Arnold] My father, he
said this is an embarrassment

00:03:02.312 --> 00:03:05.433
to me and was dumping all over me.

00:03:05.433 --> 00:03:08.250
The other thing is, you
have to work your butt off.

00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:11.265
If you think that you're
going to go accomplish

00:03:11.265 --> 00:03:13.794
something really special and be the best

00:03:13.794 --> 00:03:15.492
in anything in the world,

00:03:15.492 --> 00:03:18.371
and you think you can
do it without working,

00:03:18.371 --> 00:03:19.777
you'll make a big mistake.

00:03:19.777 --> 00:03:21.652
Because no matter what I did,

00:03:21.652 --> 00:03:23.519
if it was in body building or in acting,

00:03:23.519 --> 00:03:26.506
or in the political arena, it always took

00:03:26.506 --> 00:03:28.449
a lot a lot of work.

00:03:28.449 --> 00:03:32.824
You got to put out and you got
to make a lot of sacrifices.

00:03:32.824 --> 00:03:34.983
If you're not willing to work hard,

00:03:34.983 --> 00:03:36.882
forget about it - this is another rule

00:03:36.882 --> 00:03:38.907
that is very important.

00:03:38.907 --> 00:03:41.935
Use your power of potential
and make this nation

00:03:41.935 --> 00:03:44.036
and this world a better place.

00:03:44.036 --> 00:03:46.086
It worked for this
immigrant who came over here

00:03:46.086 --> 00:03:48.652
to this country with $20 in the pocket,

00:03:48.652 --> 00:03:52.224
and I know and I guarantee
it will work for you too.

00:03:52.224 --> 00:03:53.845
I said that I wanted to get into acting,

00:03:53.845 --> 00:03:56.129
people said "No, you have
an accent and you have

00:03:56.129 --> 00:03:58.839
a body that is too big,
and your name no one

00:03:58.839 --> 00:04:01.338
can pronounce, be realistic."

00:04:01.338 --> 00:04:03.091
It's the 70s.

00:04:03.091 --> 00:04:04.714
Today.

00:04:04.714 --> 00:04:07.547
Dustin Hoffman, he's the big shot.

00:04:08.673 --> 00:04:10.506
Al Pacino, little guy.

00:04:11.896 --> 00:04:14.614
Woody Allen, sex symbol.

00:04:14.614 --> 00:04:16.575
Even when I ran for Governor they said,

00:04:16.575 --> 00:04:21.559
"Are you kidding me, he
can never win. Give it up."

00:04:21.559 --> 00:04:23.644
But, I didn't pay any attention
because I said to myself,

00:04:23.644 --> 00:04:27.274
"What did I do when they
said you can't go to Germany,

00:04:27.274 --> 00:04:30.494
you can't compete in
the Junior Mr. Europe."

00:04:30.494 --> 00:04:32.456
I did not listen to the no.

00:04:32.456 --> 00:04:34.623
I went, and it worked out.

00:04:36.560 --> 00:04:38.541
And I used that attitude,

00:04:38.541 --> 00:04:41.791
as a blueprint for the rest of my life.

00:04:44.995 --> 00:04:46.973
Don't be afraid to fail.

00:04:46.973 --> 00:04:49.035
Because if you're afraid to fail,

00:04:49.035 --> 00:04:51.121
then you're always holding yourself back,

00:04:51.121 --> 00:04:52.397
because you're afraid if you

00:04:52.397 --> 00:04:54.434
go all out you may fail.

00:04:54.434 --> 00:04:55.857
Well, in weight lifting we learned

00:04:55.857 --> 00:04:57.442
very quickly, the only way you could break

00:04:57.442 --> 00:04:59.653
a record is if you're willing to fail.

00:04:59.653 --> 00:05:01.093
That's when you put on more weight,

00:05:01.093 --> 00:05:02.983
you try and sometimes maybe you don't,

00:05:02.983 --> 00:05:05.468
you would not be able to lift it.

00:05:05.468 --> 00:05:07.051
Which has happened to me many times.

00:05:07.051 --> 00:05:09.376
But eventually when you train hard enough,

00:05:09.376 --> 00:05:10.595
you will lift it.

00:05:10.595 --> 00:05:12.234
So, don't be afraid to fail,

00:05:12.234 --> 00:05:15.195
I mean, how far can you fall.

00:05:15.195 --> 00:05:17.317
In Austria, kids were
conditioned to follow

00:05:17.317 --> 00:05:20.918
our parents path, but, unlike other kids

00:05:20.918 --> 00:05:23.402
around me, I was very determined

00:05:23.402 --> 00:05:26.069
that I have to get out of there.

00:05:28.483 --> 00:05:30.662
And then one day, I saw the cover

00:05:30.662 --> 00:05:32.829
of a magazine of Reg Park.

00:05:33.705 --> 00:05:37.349
And it says, "How Mr.
Universe Became Hercules".

00:05:37.349 --> 00:05:40.731
I opened up this magazine
and I read through it,

00:05:40.731 --> 00:05:44.069
and it was the whole plan, laid out.

00:05:44.069 --> 00:05:47.759
I asked myself, Arnold,
what is it about you,

00:05:47.759 --> 00:05:50.162
that is so different?

00:05:50.162 --> 00:05:52.131
Why are you the only one
that sees it so clearly,

00:05:52.131 --> 00:05:54.482
the score, going to America, winning the

00:05:54.482 --> 00:05:57.245
Mr. Universe contest,
and getting into movies,

00:05:57.245 --> 00:05:59.115
and making millions of
dollars, no one else

00:05:59.115 --> 00:06:01.032
talks about this around here.

00:06:01.032 --> 00:06:03.983
Is it real? Is it just a crazy fantasy?

00:06:03.983 --> 00:06:07.168
But, wait a minute, Reg Park did it.

00:06:07.168 --> 00:06:08.679
Then it's possible.

00:06:08.679 --> 00:06:12.279
Arnold, focus. The key
thing is to be focused.

00:06:12.279 --> 00:06:14.648
Visual a goal, and I
saw myself standing up

00:06:14.648 --> 00:06:16.770
on a stage just like Reg Park

00:06:16.770 --> 00:06:19.814
and it became more and more clear.

00:06:19.814 --> 00:06:21.647
Arnold, You got to go.

00:06:24.284 --> 00:06:25.570
That just shows you again so much

00:06:25.570 --> 00:06:27.515
for it can't be done.

00:06:27.515 --> 00:06:29.056
This is what I try to tell you,

00:06:29.056 --> 00:06:31.276
anything and everything can be done

00:06:31.276 --> 00:06:33.022
if you can visualize it and if you

00:06:33.022 --> 00:06:35.109
believe in yourself.

00:06:35.109 --> 00:06:37.449
It was the same thing again
when I ran for Governor,

00:06:37.449 --> 00:06:39.617
you can imagine when I
went on the Tonight Show,

00:06:39.617 --> 00:06:41.843
and I announced that I'm going to run for

00:06:41.843 --> 00:06:44.327
Governor of the great state of California.

00:06:44.327 --> 00:06:45.660
People came to be afterwards and said,

00:06:45.660 --> 00:06:47.973
"You're crazy. You
don't announce something

00:06:47.973 --> 00:06:49.960
like this on the Tonight Show.

00:06:49.960 --> 00:06:51.759
You have an official Press Conference at

00:06:51.759 --> 00:06:54.630
the state capital. Plus, you don't start

00:06:54.630 --> 00:06:57.501
with governorship, you
start first with Mayor,

00:06:57.501 --> 00:06:59.687
or with State Senator."

00:06:59.687 --> 00:07:01.370
And I said, "I don't want to be Senator,

00:07:01.370 --> 00:07:03.108
I don't want to be Mayor.
I want to be Governor,

00:07:03.108 --> 00:07:04.556
don't you understand that?"

00:07:04.556 --> 00:07:06.301
(laughter)

00:07:06.301 --> 00:07:09.487
- Well, the rest is
history, I won in 2003,

00:07:09.487 --> 00:07:11.404
and I won also in 2006.

00:07:12.807 --> 00:07:15.275
Let me tell you, you're
going to find the naysayers

00:07:15.275 --> 00:07:17.910
in every turn you make.

00:07:17.910 --> 00:07:20.428
Don't listen, just visualize your goal,

00:07:20.428 --> 00:07:22.489
know exactly where you want to go.

00:07:22.489 --> 00:07:26.123
Trust yourself, get out
there and work like hell.

00:07:26.123 --> 00:07:27.473
And break some of the rules

00:07:27.473 --> 00:07:31.036
and never ever be afraid of failure.

00:07:31.036 --> 00:07:32.197
- Thank you guys so much for watching,

00:07:32.197 --> 00:07:34.563
I made this video because Daniel Grantham

00:07:34.563 --> 00:07:36.345
asked me to, so if there's a famous

00:07:36.345 --> 00:07:38.307
entrepreneur you want me to profile,

00:07:38.307 --> 00:07:40.215
and you want to see a top ten list of,

00:07:40.215 --> 00:07:42.268
leave their name in the comments below,

00:07:42.268 --> 00:07:44.218
and I'll see what I can do for you.

00:07:44.218 --> 00:07:45.602
Now, Arnold liked to talk a lot about

00:07:45.602 --> 00:07:47.554
how important it is to have a clear goal

00:07:47.554 --> 00:07:49.526
that's set out and achieve for yourself,

00:07:49.526 --> 00:07:51.441
so my question of the day for you today

00:07:51.441 --> 00:07:53.657
is what is your clear goal?

00:07:53.657 --> 00:07:54.780
What is a clear goal that you,

00:07:54.780 --> 00:07:56.993
you're trying to work towards,

00:07:56.993 --> 00:07:58.900
to build that life and that business

00:07:58.900 --> 00:08:00.232
for yourself? Leave in the comments,

00:08:00.232 --> 00:08:01.865
I'd love to hear from you.

00:08:01.865 --> 00:08:03.157
And of course if you like this video

00:08:03.157 --> 00:08:04.022
and you want to see more,

00:08:04.022 --> 00:08:05.549
don't forget to subscribe
to the newsletter

00:08:05.549 --> 00:08:06.890
and to the channel and I hope

00:08:06.890 --> 00:08:08.682
to see you again tomorrow morning

00:08:08.682 --> 00:08:10.635
for another shot of entrepreneurship

00:08:10.635 --> 00:08:12.819
to kickstart your day,
thank you for watching

00:08:12.819 --> 00:08:15.277
continue to believe,
and I'll see you soon.

00:08:15.277 --> 00:08:17.360
(swoosh)

